INFO 4492 title=Page 51 | len=902 | 4.45 P. M New York Mar 10th 1864 New York 10th for G. V. Fox Wash'n Cant possibly come tonight may perhaps tomorrow night Store keeper Marsh = shals clerk Kelsey has disappeared & taken the memorandum books most valuable I expect more will abscond watch your yard closely have Ford Koonz chief clerk of Navy Agent Wash'n locked up in old Capital & make care = ful search for his private letters  watch Georg || w is suspicious You had better direct Navy Yards here or elsewhere to purchase temporarily in open market of leading houses . Hiram Ketchum & other lawyers want to see prisoners as counsel I have promised to get your instructions by tomorrow sig H S Olcott Special Comnr 
