INFO 10194 title=Page 52 | len=791 | 2.30 Pm New York Mar 11th 1864 New York March 11th for G. V. Fox Wash'n Telegram received good cause to arrest Brown a master black = smith Wash'n Yard also Jenks a clerk who weighs metals and several others I wont give any names until we meet tomorrow. dont think it safe  to write particulars about Keeler period Dont want to arrest any here until all are arrested for it would spoil our plans sig H S Olcott  || so Jenks a clerk who weighs metals and several others I wont give any names until we meet tomorrow. dont think it safe  to write particulars about Keeler period Dont want to arrest any here until all are arrested for it would spoil our plans sig H S Olcott Special Comn'r &c   Geo D Sheldon Ft Monroe  Head Qrs A of P Mar 11th 1864 For Capt McEntee with Genl Kilpatrick . The Genl Commanding desires you to return to Hd Qrs with such of our men as are not hurt if Genl Kilpatrick is not comming immediately you will come by  way of Washington transportation will be furnished you on application by Co
